{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy this file to appsettings.json in this directory and fill it in.",
    "appsettings.json is gitignored by **/*appsettings.json; this .example is not, because the",
    "pattern ends at .json. Keep it that way: this file must never hold a real key.",
    "THE Google BLOCK IS NOT OPTIONAL FOR A GOOGLE AGENT PLATFORM KEY.", 
    "Leave the Google block out entirely for an ordinary Developer API key."
  ],
  "ApiKeys": {
    "AmazonBedrock": "",
    "GoogleAgentPlatform": ""
  },
  "Google": {
    "Enterprise": true,
    "Project": "your-project-id",
    "Location": "global"
  },

  "_model_comment": [
    "The model each provider runs when --llm names none. Optional: without it, Gemini runs",
    "gemini-2.5-flash and Bedrock the Strands SDK's default. One per provider, because a model id",
    "means nothing to the other one; --llm overrides either. Gemini has its own block rather than",
    "sharing Google's, because the Google block is left out for an ordinary Developer API key.",
    "`anchor check --full --provider auto` runs whatever is configured here, and stops before the",
    "run, after a one-token test request, if it cannot be reached."
  ],
  "Gemini": {
    "Model": "gemini-2.5-flash"
  },

  "_bedrock_comment": [
    "Bedrock takes its API key as a BEARER TOKEN in the environment, not as a constructor",
    "argument: botocore builds the name from the service's signing name, so it reads",
    "AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK. ApiKeys:AmazonBedrock above is put there for you.",
    "",
    "REGION IS REQUIRED when you authenticate with a key, the same way the Google block is",
    "required for an Agent Platform key. With a key we do not read ~/.aws at all, so there is no",
    "profile for the region to come from. It also decides which models exist. AWS_REGION works too.",
    "",
    "Why ~/.aws is not read: create_client resolves the credential chain BEFORE consulting the",
    "bearer token and then discards it, because bearer auth supersedes SigV4 at signing. Walking",
    "the chain can only fail, never help -- a [default] profile with login_session reaches a",
    "CRT-backed provider and dies with 'pip install botocore[crt]' over a value nothing would have",
    "used. So with a key the client is pointed at os.devnull for both AWS config files.",
    "",
    "Profile is for naming a DIFFERENT ACCOUNT, and most people should leave it empty. Naming one",
    "turns the above off and reads ~/.aws normally. It is NOT an authentication setting while a key",
    "is present -- the token supersedes whatever the profile yields, so an expired profile and a",
    "working one behave identically, which is how one sat unnoticed with dead keys for an afternoon.",
    "",
    "UseAwsConfig forces the question: true always reads ~/.aws, false never does. Leave it out.",
    "",
    "Streaming false is needed by some models. ai21.jamba-1-5-large answers 'This model doesn't",
    "support tool use in streaming mode', and this agent is nothing but tool use. Anthropic and",
    "Nova models stream tools fine, so leave it out unless a model complains. --no-stream is the",
    "command-line equivalent."
  ],
  "Bedrock": {
    "Region": "us-east-1",
    "Profile": "",
    "Streaming": true,
    "Model": ""
  }
}
